kernel-sh2-j2.img: Linux 6.18.37 for the J-Core J2 (sh2eb, no MMU)
==================================================================

Runs on the J2 machine of the uclibc-ng qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
branch uclibc-ng, hw/sh4/j2.c), which follows the Numato Mimas V2 device
tree:

  qemu-system-sh4eb -M j2 -m 256M -nographic -kernel kernel.img -initrd rootfs.img

The board passes its own device tree and the memory size from -m; the
command line comes from the kernel (console=ttyUL0 earlycon).

Rebuilding
----------

  tar -xaf linux-6.18.37.tar.xz && cd linux-6.18.37
  patch -p1 < kernel-sh2-j2.patch
  cp kernel-sh2-j2.config .config
  make ARCH=sh CROSS_COMPILE=sh2eb-openadk-linux-uclibc- olddefconfig vmlinux
  sh2eb-openadk-linux-uclibc-objcopy -R .reginfo -R .notes -R .note -R .comment \
      -R .mdebug -R .note.gnu.build-id -S vmlinux kernel-sh2-j2.img

The config is j2_defconfig plus BLK_DEV_INITRD, RD_GZIP, RD_XZ, TMPFS and
PRINT_FATAL_SIGNALS.

The toolchain has to be a J2 one: openadk system numato-mimasv2 (CPU j2,
-mj2, binutils 2.42, gcc 10.5.0; built from lordrasmus/openadk 76066e919).
j2_defconfig has SMP, and the SMP code uses the J2-only cas.l, which the
generic sh2 toolchain the CI builds uClibc-ng with (-m2, binutils 2.39)
does not assemble.

Two things that look like options but are not:

- Without SMP, 6.18 does not boot on J2: it stops in pcpu_setup_first_chunk
  with "percpu: can't handle more than one group" and kernel BUG at
  mm/percpu.c:2591, before the console comes up.
- Without the __ffs() part of the patch, a gcc-10 build hangs after
  "SMP: Total of 1 processors activated" (see the patch header).

The userland is FLAT; it needs the BINFMT_FLAT_NO_DATA_START_OFFSET part of
the patch, otherwise every program with a GOT crashes right after start.
